  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian Red Cross Partnership - global humanitarian preparedness and response programs  2019-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Red Cross - DFAT Humanitarian Partnership Program supports nine Red Cross Red Crescent National Societies in the Pacific (Fiji, Tonga, PNG, Solomon Islands, and Vanautu) and Asia (Timor-Leste, Indonesia, Myanmar and Mongolia) to prepare for, respond to and recover from disasters. The program takes a locally-led approach and provides core cost support, technical assistance to enable organisational strengthening and improved disaster response capabilities and support for their role as auxiliary to government. The Partnership helps support climate change adaptation, women&apos;s leadership and disability inclusion via its activities.</narrative>
  </description>
